WEBVTT

00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:03.600
I'm definitely gonna be the first-star idol!

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:07.570
Nijino Yume's about to start her Aikatsu!

00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:14.240
Aikatsu Island was held once again this year on a tropical island.

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:17.240
We raised the roof with our S4 performance,

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:19.540
and all three days were a blast.

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:24.040
Now that it's over, we've got a day off.

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:27.880
Since we were already here, we decided to go have some fun in the ocean.

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:30.920
I wonder if we'll see a sea turtle.

00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:32.590
I'd love to swim with it.

00:00:32.590 --> 00:00:34.130
That sounds cool.

00:00:41.810 --> 00:00:44.020
Fog? You're kidding.

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:48.860
We'll be fine, right?

00:00:48.860 --> 00:00:51.030
Of course we will!

00:00:59.370 --> 00:01:01.040
Thank goodness.

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:03.790
Hey, where are we?

00:01:03.790 --> 00:01:06.750
Oh no! We drifted out to sea!

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:09.040
Look! It's an island!

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:15.550
<i>Our exciting day looks to be taking an unexpected turn!</i>

00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:27.850
We managed to make it somehow.

00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:32.110
I don't think this water will last us.

00:01:33.070 --> 00:01:35.280
Let's go secure a water source first.

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:36.360
Okay.

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:44.370
I'm getting a really bad feeling about this.

00:01:44.750 --> 00:01:47.620
It's just your imagination. Don't freak us out.

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:15.650
That gave me a scare.

00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:18.450
Wait. Which way did we come from?

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:21.030
No idea.

00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:24.040
Sorry, I shouldn't have screamed like that.

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:25.790
It's not your fault.

00:02:25.790 --> 00:02:26.370
But—

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:30.830
Do you hear that?

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:34.210
It's water!

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:37.420
Good job, Yume-chan!

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:40.760
I only found it because you ran us out here.

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:42.260
Nice, Koharu!

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:43.760
Really now...

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:46.850
All right, I'll go check it out.

00:02:51.190 --> 00:02:51.650
Yume!

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:09.160
Thank you.

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:10.670
Are you okay?

00:03:10.670 --> 00:03:11.830
Yes.

00:03:12.330 --> 00:03:13.380
Who are you?

00:03:13.380 --> 00:03:17.000
I'm Hoshimiya Ichigo. Glad you're not hurt!

00:03:21.010 --> 00:03:23.140
We're here!

00:03:24.220 --> 00:03:26.390
Is this your place?

00:03:26.390 --> 00:03:28.600
Yep! Fabulous, isn't it?

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:31.190
Yes, it's such a charming tent!

00:03:33.650 --> 00:03:36.610
Wh-Whoa, did I go overboard?

00:03:36.610 --> 00:03:38.780
It's fine, Ichigo will eat them.

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:40.900
Aoi! Ran!

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:42.610
Welcome back!

00:03:42.610 --> 00:03:43.910
Thanks!

00:03:43.910 --> 00:03:47.160
Who are those girls with Ichigo?

00:03:52.330 --> 00:03:53.670
You three!

00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:55.540
You have the scent of idols!

00:03:56.630 --> 00:03:57.590
Really?

00:03:57.590 --> 00:03:58.500
Yes.

00:03:58.500 --> 00:04:01.050
But what are you doing all the way out here?

00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:03.800
To be honest, we got lost at sea.

00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:08.930
And then after we got here, 
Hoshimiya-san saved me from danger.

00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:11.310
Oh no, that sounds awful.

00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:13.940
Drink up this coconut water to start with. {we never gave Ran a standard translation for this particular line}

00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:15.690
Thank you!

00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:22.320
So good!

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:24.070
Have you calmed down? {it's like, this is so clearly right, yet because of how much time has passed it feels awkward}

00:04:24.070 --> 00:04:24.990
Yes.

00:04:24.990 --> 00:04:28.830
By the way, what brings the rest of you to this island?

00:04:28.830 --> 00:04:32.250
To put it simply, we're practicing self-sufficiency on an uninhabited island.

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:34.330
We're doing it for a TV program.

00:04:34.330 --> 00:04:35.960
What? A TV program?

00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:38.340
It's been about a week now.

00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:41.380
We ran into a crocodile in the Amazon just the other day.

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:44.050
We're adventuring in the uncharted nooks of the world!

00:04:45.470 --> 00:04:48.010
It's a bit crazy to think about.

00:04:48.970 --> 00:04:53.230
I guess we were really lucky to run into pro adventurers like you.

00:04:53.230 --> 00:04:54.940
Pro adventurers...

00:04:54.940 --> 00:04:57.270
If you think so, then maybe we are.

00:04:57.270 --> 00:05:01.730
Just between us, we're not the only pro adventurers on this island.

00:05:01.730 --> 00:05:05.110
Right, but we won't lose to our rivals in Tristar!

00:05:05.110 --> 00:05:08.240
Yeah, we of Soleil will be the victors!

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:10.830
Tristar? Soleil?

00:05:10.830 --> 00:05:12.750
I cannot let that pass unchallenged.

00:05:13.290 --> 00:05:18.750
Thinking you could possibly beat us? Somebody sounds eager to have their blood sucked by Yurika-sama.

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:22.300
That's right! Tristar is unbeatable!

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:23.800
Right, Mizuki?

00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:25.550
Exactly.

00:05:25.550 --> 00:05:30.300
Tristar will emerge victorious and claim the prize.

00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:33.270
The race begins at noon tomorrow.

00:05:33.270 --> 00:05:37.900
Whoever manages to reach land first on the boat they make will claim victory.

00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:38.730
Almost ready?

00:05:38.730 --> 00:05:41.360
Yep! We're not gonna lose!

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:43.900
Whose side are you girls on?

00:05:43.900 --> 00:05:46.400
Ours or Soleil's?

00:05:47.150 --> 00:05:49.910
We're going to take part too?

00:05:49.910 --> 00:05:52.950
Join us, and we'll catch you some fresh fish...

00:05:54.290 --> 00:05:56.410
And roll up some sushi.

00:05:56.410 --> 00:05:57.790
Sushi?!

00:05:57.790 --> 00:05:59.080
I want some too!

00:05:59.080 --> 00:06:01.290
Don't get reeled in, Ichigo.

00:06:01.290 --> 00:06:03.170
We need to compete with something.

00:06:03.170 --> 00:06:04.670
If you join us...

00:06:04.670 --> 00:06:09.470
We'll treat you to an extra-large parfait filled to the brim with bananas!

00:06:09.470 --> 00:06:11.350
Extra-large banana parfaits?!

00:06:11.350 --> 00:06:13.390
I can't choose!

00:06:13.390 --> 00:06:15.640
Only one thing to do!

00:06:16.180 --> 00:06:17.350
Draw lots!

00:06:18.190 --> 00:06:19.810
And, pull!

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:24.480
The Soleil team gets Yume-chan and Koharu-chan!

00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:25.780
Let's do this.

00:06:25.780 --> 00:06:27.150
Yeah!

00:06:27.150 --> 00:06:30.570
The Tristar team gets Rola-chan. Glad to have you.

00:06:30.570 --> 00:06:32.530
Thanks! I'll do my best.

00:06:32.530 --> 00:06:35.290
Now to recommence the boat making!

00:06:40.630 --> 00:06:44.800
Oh, so you're an idol from Four Star Academy.

00:06:44.800 --> 00:06:49.720
Not only do you have your own brand, but you design dresses too... that's something special.

00:06:50.640 --> 00:06:52.430
Thank you.

00:06:52.430 --> 00:06:55.350
Okay, so what's your dream, Yume-chan?

00:06:55.350 --> 00:06:56.890
My dream is...

00:06:58.140 --> 00:07:02.150
I want to be the world's brightest idol, I guess. {adapted from ep 59}

00:07:02.150 --> 00:07:04.110
Wow, the world's brightest!

00:07:04.110 --> 00:07:08.280
But before that, there's something I absolutely have to get.

00:07:08.280 --> 00:07:11.160
It's just that I don't have the ability at the moment.

00:07:11.820 --> 00:07:13.160
Is that troubling you?

00:07:14.780 --> 00:07:17.750
Even so, I can't let that stop me.

00:07:17.750 --> 00:07:20.790
I'm doing everything I can right now.

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:24.670
That's the way. Positivity is the best!

00:07:24.670 --> 00:07:25.920
Yes!

00:07:28.920 --> 00:07:31.800
All right, that's done. Let's take a break.

00:07:31.800 --> 00:07:32.680
Okay.

00:07:34.470 --> 00:07:35.680
Ran-san.

00:07:36.560 --> 00:07:39.850
Have you three been in a team for a long time?

00:07:39.850 --> 00:07:42.770
Yeah, for quite a while now.

00:07:42.770 --> 00:07:47.400
We do pretty much everything together, 
and being with them fills me with confidence.

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:49.320
You sure seem close.

00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:50.570
We are.

00:07:50.570 --> 00:07:56.080
There was a time when we couldn't be together, 
but afterwards our bonds grew stronger than before.

00:07:56.080 --> 00:07:57.620
That's reassuring!

00:07:57.620 --> 00:08:02.370
I've actually been studying abroad, and I only just came back recently.

00:08:02.370 --> 00:08:08.550
It's made me really appreciate doing Aikatsu with Yume-chan and the others.

00:08:08.550 --> 00:08:11.550
I understand what you're feeling.

00:08:11.550 --> 00:08:17.810
Being away for a while strengthened my conviction that my place was with Ichigo and Aoi.

00:08:17.810 --> 00:08:18.810
Yeah.

00:08:18.810 --> 00:08:22.810
I think that the time we spend apart isn't time wasted.

00:08:22.810 --> 00:08:23.890
I agree.

00:08:26.610 --> 00:08:28.690
Yozora-senpai's scent...

00:08:30.860 --> 00:08:34.860
Ran-san, you smell like the senpai I admire.

00:08:34.860 --> 00:08:36.570
Do I?

00:08:36.570 --> 00:08:39.450
It's an honor to be put on the same level as her.

00:08:40.950 --> 00:08:42.910
Heave-ho!

00:08:45.370 --> 00:08:47.210
We've finished this side.

00:08:47.210 --> 00:08:49.040
Almost done over here.

00:08:53.090 --> 00:08:54.430
Good work.

00:08:55.470 --> 00:08:56.970
Thank you.

00:08:57.890 --> 00:09:02.390
So you're an idol, Rola-chan? Is Aikatsu fun?

00:09:02.390 --> 00:09:04.190
Yes, of course!

00:09:04.190 --> 00:09:10.150
I've been through a lot, but I believe the path I chose wasn't a mistake.

00:09:10.480 --> 00:09:11.860
I see.

00:09:11.860 --> 00:09:17.360
Still, I only managed to get this far thanks to having Yume as my rival.

00:09:17.870 --> 00:09:19.200
You're blessed.

00:09:20.580 --> 00:09:23.830
People tend to set their own limitations.

00:09:23.830 --> 00:09:29.340
That's why having someone close by to show you your potential is truly fortunate.

00:09:30.170 --> 00:09:31.000
Yes!

00:09:31.840 --> 00:09:33.840
Yay!

00:09:33.840 --> 00:09:35.220
It's complete!

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:39.300
I'd call this a pretty nice boat.

00:09:39.300 --> 00:09:42.220
Yeah. Tomorrow's race is in the bag.

00:09:42.220 --> 00:09:46.100
Yume-chan, Koharu-chan, thanks so much for helping us!

00:09:46.100 --> 00:09:49.060
I'm glad we were able to repay you for saving us.

00:09:49.060 --> 00:09:51.110
I hope you win tomorrow.

00:09:51.110 --> 00:09:52.070
Ichigo.

00:09:52.730 --> 00:09:55.240
Our boat is ready too.

00:09:55.240 --> 00:09:57.660
We'll be coming out on top tomorrow.

00:09:57.660 --> 00:09:59.410
Better be prepared!

00:09:59.410 --> 00:10:02.620
I may not be able to sleep tonight due to the anticipation.

00:10:02.620 --> 00:10:07.580
Speaking of tonight, I'd like to start getting ready for our last event on the island!

00:10:07.580 --> 00:10:09.040
What event?

00:10:09.040 --> 00:10:10.630
What else could it be?

00:10:10.630 --> 00:10:12.630
The campfire!

00:10:12.630 --> 00:10:14.260
Campfire!

00:10:14.260 --> 00:10:15.760
That sounds like fun!

00:10:15.760 --> 00:10:19.510
Without any further ado, let's get chopping!

00:10:19.510 --> 00:10:20.800
I figured...

00:10:20.800 --> 00:10:22.470
Of course.

00:10:39.780 --> 00:10:43.370
It's been a while since I've seen Ichigo holding an axe.

00:10:43.370 --> 00:10:44.700
That's awesome!

00:10:44.700 --> 00:10:46.910
Yep, it's something special!

00:10:47.000 --> 00:10:49.040
Here I go!

00:10:55.800 --> 00:10:57.300
Wow!

00:10:57.300 --> 00:10:58.970
Yume-chan, wanna try?

00:10:58.970 --> 00:11:00.090
I can?

00:11:00.630 --> 00:11:01.800
Sure!

00:11:07.100 --> 00:11:08.980
It tingles!

00:11:10.940 --> 00:11:12.270
Let's take turns.

00:11:12.270 --> 00:11:13.980
Okay...

00:11:20.610 --> 00:11:22.620
One, two!

00:11:26.740 --> 00:11:28.120
Yay!

00:11:33.790 --> 00:11:35.000
It's so pretty.

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:35.840
Yeah.

00:11:37.170 --> 00:11:38.920
I'm getting hungry.

00:11:38.920 --> 00:11:40.050
Me too.

00:11:40.050 --> 00:11:41.510
You did work hard.{uh... fine}{it was a mistake, okay}

00:11:41.510 --> 00:11:43.260
They should be done soon.

00:11:43.260 --> 00:11:45.050
Hey, everyone!

00:11:45.050 --> 00:11:46.930
Yes! Kaede Sushi! {I'm only 95% sure or so about this spelling}{I'm like 97% sure}

00:11:46.930 --> 00:11:50.310
Tropical delicious fish. Bon appetit!

00:11:50.310 --> 00:11:52.310
It looks delicious!

00:11:52.310 --> 00:11:54.020
Please enjoy.

00:11:54.020 --> 00:11:57.730
Be sure to eat your fill. I'm not the chef, though.

00:11:57.730 --> 00:11:59.820
Yes! Leave it to me!

00:11:59.820 --> 00:12:01.530
Don't mind if I do!

00:12:05.700 --> 00:12:07.330
It's delicious!

00:12:07.330 --> 00:12:10.250
I've never had sushi this good before!

00:12:10.250 --> 00:12:12.210
My cheeks are melting! {I don't... know English anymore}{this is as fine as anything I guess}

00:12:12.210 --> 00:12:15.710
Naturally. I caught the fish myself.

00:12:15.710 --> 00:12:18.630
Says the person who almost drowned when a sea cucumber scared her.

00:12:18.630 --> 00:12:20.460
Don't tell them that!

00:12:20.460 --> 00:12:22.840
Here, have some too.

00:12:22.840 --> 00:12:26.260
They all look so good! I don't know where to begin! {if B, then A}

00:12:26.260 --> 00:12:28.720
Why not just start with one of each?

00:12:28.720 --> 00:12:30.470
That's the way!

00:12:30.470 --> 00:12:31.310
So good!

00:12:31.310 --> 00:12:32.480
But which first?

00:12:32.850 --> 00:12:34.600
Alan, it's supper time.

00:12:35.230 --> 00:12:37.310
I picked these fruits in the forest.{we could probably use berry}

00:12:41.610 --> 00:12:43.150
So cute!

00:12:43.150 --> 00:12:44.610
Is he a bat?

00:12:44.610 --> 00:12:47.660
That's right. Berries are his favorite.

00:13:12.270 --> 00:13:14.730
We'll have to delay the start time.

00:13:14.730 --> 00:13:17.400
It's just a squall, so it'll pass soon.

00:13:17.400 --> 00:13:19.270
Alan!

00:13:19.610 --> 00:13:21.780
Alan!

00:13:21.780 --> 00:13:23.690
Alan!

00:13:23.690 --> 00:13:25.740
Yurika-chan, what's wrong?

00:13:25.740 --> 00:13:27.280
Alan went missing.

00:13:27.280 --> 00:13:28.240
What?!

00:13:28.240 --> 00:13:31.410
My group is out looking for him elsewhere.

00:13:31.950 --> 00:13:33.830
We'll go search too!

00:13:35.830 --> 00:13:37.420
Alan!

00:13:37.420 --> 00:13:39.000
Alan!

00:13:39.000 --> 00:13:40.670
Alan!

00:13:40.670 --> 00:13:43.170
Alan!

00:13:46.470 --> 00:13:48.090
Alan!

00:13:54.310 --> 00:13:55.730
A berry bush! {tree if you want}{I don't want}

00:13:55.730 --> 00:13:57.140
I'll be right back!

00:13:58.480 --> 00:14:00.560
Aikatsu!

00:14:00.560 --> 00:14:02.570
Wow!

00:14:12.080 --> 00:14:14.580
Were you taking shelter from the rain?

00:14:14.580 --> 00:14:16.660
Did you find him?

00:14:16.660 --> 00:14:18.830
He's up here!

00:14:19.960 --> 00:14:21.170
Yume-chan!

00:14:21.840 --> 00:14:25.090
Do you want to climb with me to the top?

00:14:27.090 --> 00:14:28.090
Yurika!

00:14:28.090 --> 00:14:29.590
Did you find him?

00:14:41.230 --> 00:14:42.860
She found him!

00:14:42.860 --> 00:14:43.900
What a relief.

00:14:43.900 --> 00:14:45.110
Yes!

00:14:45.110 --> 00:14:47.360
I'm so glad for you.

00:14:47.360 --> 00:14:51.870
Aikatsu! Aikatsu!

00:14:52.320 --> 00:14:54.540
Aikatsu!

00:14:54.870 --> 00:14:57.330
Aikatsu!

00:14:57.330 --> 00:15:06.130
Aikatsu! Aikatsu! Aikatsu!

00:15:14.600 --> 00:15:16.470
Amazing!

00:15:16.470 --> 00:15:19.850
I love climbing cliffs.

00:15:19.850 --> 00:15:21.560
Why's that?

00:15:21.560 --> 00:15:23.110
At the end of your climb...

00:15:24.360 --> 00:15:27.530
An incredible view awaits you.

00:15:27.530 --> 00:15:28.490
I guess!

00:15:29.240 --> 00:15:30.530
I understand!

00:15:35.530 --> 00:15:39.040
I'm definitely gonna be the world's brightest idol!

00:15:42.290 --> 00:15:44.540
Set sail!

00:15:57.260 --> 00:15:59.680
Soleil versus Tristar!

00:15:59.680 --> 00:16:04.230
Soleil triumphs in the idol uninhabited island contest!{we could totally switch idol and uninhabited island, something something lovely my angel}

00:16:04.230 --> 00:16:05.690
We did it!

00:16:05.690 --> 00:16:09.320
We get to perform as Soleil as our reward!

00:16:09.320 --> 00:16:10.860
Looks like we lost.

00:16:10.860 --> 00:16:12.320
I'm disappointed.

00:16:12.320 --> 00:16:14.950
But it was a very, very fun race!

00:16:14.950 --> 00:16:16.580
Idols?

00:16:16.580 --> 00:16:18.330
Yume-chan, thank you!

00:16:18.330 --> 00:16:20.450
You're all idols too?

00:16:20.450 --> 00:16:21.290
Yeah.

00:16:21.290 --> 00:16:22.580
What a surprise!

00:16:22.580 --> 00:16:26.080
Since you're already here, stay and watch our show!

00:16:26.080 --> 00:16:27.090
Of course!

00:16:28.750 --> 00:16:30.340
Are you ready?

00:16:30.340 --> 00:16:33.010
Let's put on the best show we can!

00:16:33.010 --> 00:16:35.510
Yeah, we'll make it something special!

00:16:35.510 --> 00:16:38.810
Right, we'll entertain them to the fullest!

00:16:38.810 --> 00:16:40.270
Here we go!

00:16:40.270 --> 00:16:42.980
Soleil Rising!

00:19:46.080 --> 00:19:47.160
Whoa...

00:19:47.160 --> 00:19:48.330
I know!

00:19:48.330 --> 00:19:50.660
I'm feeling kinda hyped up!

00:19:50.660 --> 00:19:53.130
I wish I could take the stage too.

00:19:53.130 --> 00:19:54.840
Great idea.

00:19:54.840 --> 00:19:57.670
I'd like to see you perform too.

00:19:58.510 --> 00:20:00.010
Me too!

00:20:00.010 --> 00:20:02.340
Huh? That uniform...

00:20:02.340 --> 00:20:05.600
We've gotta expand the Aikatsu ring! {I think I allowed this once}

00:20:05.600 --> 00:20:06.850
Hang on...

00:20:06.850 --> 00:20:09.140
Akari-chan taught it to me!

00:20:09.140 --> 00:20:11.850
Akari-chan?! You know her? {this is the second time I think Yume has been deliberately made stupider, but a different episode writer}

00:20:11.850 --> 00:20:14.860
She's a few years below us at our school.

00:20:14.860 --> 00:20:18.400
Does that mean the Hoshimiya-senpai she mentioned...

00:20:19.030 --> 00:20:20.610
I see now.

00:20:20.610 --> 00:20:23.360
Go on, the crowd is waiting.

00:20:23.360 --> 00:20:25.620
Go out and shine your brightest!

00:20:26.200 --> 00:20:27.030
I will!

00:22:47.090 --> 00:22:50.680
Your passionate Aikatsu was wonderful!

00:22:50.680 --> 00:22:53.640
So was yours! I'm so happy to have met you, Ichigo-chan. {just wait one fucking second, you can't call her that}{she's free from the oppressive hierarchy, bitches}

00:22:53.640 --> 00:22:56.560
Let's both keep working hard at our Aikatsu.

00:22:57.680 --> 00:22:58.640
Okay!

00:22:59.350 --> 00:23:04.270
Aikatsu is so much fun I can't contain my excitement!

00:24:06.340 --> 00:24:11.930
Soleil's Star Sunshine Coords and performance were so amazing, they're something special!

00:24:11.930 --> 00:24:14.930
Yeah, yeah! That too is Aikatsu!

00:24:14.930 --> 00:24:18.770
Connect to the future with the Aikatsu ring!

00:24:21.020 --> 00:24:22.270
The ship's setting sail?

00:24:22.270 --> 00:24:24.020
Our study there is over?

00:24:24.020 --> 00:24:26.610
Does that mean we'll have to part ways again?

00:24:27.400 --> 00:24:29.530
Next time on Aikatsu Stars!

00:24:29.530 --> 00:24:31.240
Goodbye, Koharu-chan. {dropped}{I didn't realize you liked kirara that much}

00:24:31.240 --> 00:24:33.660
Become the first-star idol!
